@!internal
module nupp.runtime.seam.browsercryptosuite

--[[
The one seam whose suite asserts nothing beyond its shape.

Everything `host.browser_crypto` promises is the host's -- WebCrypto's digest,
its random bytes, its identifiers -- so a vector here would assert what a
browser does rather than what a provider does, and it would have to reach a
browser to do it. `nupp.runtime.seam.module` checks the shape before calling
this, which is the whole of what a loaded module can be held to.

This was the `validate` call the seam's own factory published. The factory is
gone and the check it forwarded to now runs ahead of every suite, so the
forwarding was the only thing left in it.
]]

local suite = {}

@allow("unused-binding")
function suite.test(provider: any): (boolean, string?)
    return true
end

export = suite
